---
description: Frontend code conventions for this Nuxt + Three.js portfolio
globs: app/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Code conventions for this project are defined in @AGENTS.md.

Follow them for every `.vue`, `.ts` and `.css` file under `app/`: build scenes
through `useLesson`, always tear a scene down in `onUnmounted` (cancel the tick,
dispose geometries/materials/textures/renderer, clear timers and listeners), size
the canvas from its container rather than the window, keep lesson pages thin by
moving heavy logic into `composables/three-js-lessons/`, register every new
lesson in `useLessons.ts`, give each page its SEO `useHead` block, use
`<script setup lang="ts">` and avoid `any`, reuse the `.btn` / `.card` Tailwind
component classes instead of new raw hex values, reserve `handle*` names for
event handlers, and delete dead or commented-out code.
